# An Interactive Journey Through the Finite Báez–Duarte Transform

Begin with the central change of viewpoint: an alternating binomial transform of reciprocal moments is a collection of independently decaying arithmetic modes. Move the sliders below to see how the integer $n$ controls both amplitude and persistence.

