<details><summary>Reveal the exact finite identity and proof</summary>
For $M_j(N)=\sum_{n=1}^N\mu(n)n^{-2j-2}$ and $C_k(N)=\sum_{j=0}^k(-1)^j inom{k}{j}M_j(N)$, exchanging finite sums and applying $\sum_j(-1)^j inom{k}{j}x^j=(1-x)^k$ gives $C_k(N)=\sum_{n=1}^N\mu(n)n^{-2}(1-n^{-2})^k$.
</details>

## Positive weights

When all weights are nonnegative, every mode is nonnegative and decays. The complete sum therefore stays nonnegative and decreases.

