<details><summary>Reveal the finite-difference hierarchy</summary>
A forward difference sends $r^k$ to $-(1-r)r^k$. Here $1-r_n=n^{-2}$, so $(-1)^q\Delta^qC_k=\sum_n\mu(n)n^{-2q-2}(1-n^{-2})^k$. Nonnegative weights make every right-hand side nonnegative.
</details>

